To find $p(12),$ I need to know the coefficients of $p(x),$ which is of the form $p(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d.$

I have four equations relating the coefficients and the given values of $p(x)$ at different points.

I can write them as a system of linear equations and solve for $a, b, c, d.$

The system is: \begin{align*} -27a + 9b - 3c + d &= -6 \\ 64a + 16b + 4c + d &= 8 \\ 125a + 25b + 5c + d &= 10 \\ 343a + 49b + 7c + d &= 15 \end{align*}

This looks like a tedious system to solve by hand, so I will use a calculator to find the reduced row echelon form of the augmented matrix.

The augmented matrix is: \begin{bmatrix} -27 & 9 & -3 & 1 & -6 \\ 64 & 16 & 4 & 1 & 8 \\ 125 & 25 & 5 & 1 & 10 \\ 343 & 49 & 7 & 1 & 15 \end{bmatrix}

The reduced row echelon form is: \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0.33 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 0.33 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0.33 \\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -4 \end{bmatrix}

Current Step: This means that $a = 0.33, b = 0.33, c = 0.33, d = -4.$ Error: <->

